.TH OROC-TOOLING-SWIFT 1 "" "Oro Runtime 0.2.1" "Oro Runtime Manual"
.SH NAME
oroc\-tooling\-swift \- Export Swift compiler commands and prepare analysis modules.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
oroc tooling swift [options] [<project\-dir>]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Export Swift compiler commands and prepare analysis modules.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-platform=<name>\fR
desktop, mac, ios, ios\-simulator, linux or win
.TP
\fB\-\-arch=<name>\fR
target architecture
.TP
\fB\-\-prod\fR
select release compiler flags
.TP
\fB\-\-prepare\fR
emit the declared Swift module without linking or signing
.TP
\fB\-\-refresh\fR
allocate a fresh editor generation
.TP
\fB\-\-offline\fR
use installed toolchains and dependencies only
.TP
\fB\-\-config=<path>\fR
use an explicit oro.toml or oro.ini
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
show help
.SH NOTES
.PP
Declare original sources and module settings under tooling.swift, or import an existing compilation database.
.PP
Apple targets require macOS and Xcode. External build systems own their dependency preparation.
.PP
Use language_server.swift.adapter="stdio" for native SwiftPM discovery.
.PP
See docs/LANGUAGE_SERVER.md for configuration and editor examples.
.SH SEE ALSO
oroc(1), oroc\-tooling(1)
